    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a sharp spike (e.g., Example 4 where price jumped from ~85 to 89); forecasts fail to account for the volatility of the spike and instead predict a smooth continuation.",
    "Forecasts display significant mean reversion lag; they underestimate the immediate drop after a spike (e.g., Example 1, Day 2) and overestimate the recovery time required to stabilize near historical averages.",
    "Sentiment spikes (0.33) correlate with model failure to predict sudden volatility events; high sentiment days often precede sharp price reversals rather than sustained trends.",
    "Model assumes linear growth in response to positive sentiment, ignoring the non-linear 'sell-off' behavior seen when prices exceed recent highs by >5%.",
    "Forecast horizon is too long-term relative to market microstructure; short-term corrections (within 3-5 days) are consistently missed while long-term averages remain accurate."
  ]
